WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.224
The Chauri Chaura incident took place on 4
February 1922 in Gorakhpur district.

2
00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:21.544
Three civilians and 22 policemen died in the
incident.

3
00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:29.744
Gandhi halted the non-cooperation movement on
the national level on 12 February 1922.

4
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.989
The non-cooperation movement was launched on 4
September 1920

5
00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:41.976
to withdraw cooperation from the British
government.

6
00:00:42.256 --> 00:00:49.096
A protest against the police was called on 4
February, to be held at the bazaar.

7
00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:57.416
Approximately 2,000 to 2,500 protesters
assembled and marched towards the market lane.

8
00:00:57.696 --> 00:01:03.264
A police officer had attacked volunteers
picketing a liquor shop.

9
00:01:03.544 --> 00:01:09.904
Several of the leaders were arrested and put
in the lock-up at the police station.

10
00:01:10.184 --> 00:01:16.724
Armed police were dispatched while the
protesters marched towards the bazaar,

11
00:01:16.784 --> 00:01:18.584
shouting anti-British slogans.

12
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.872
Gupteshwar Singh ordered his 15 local police
officers to fire warning shots into the air.

13
00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:40.064
The warning shots only agitated the crowd,
which began to throw stones at the police.

14
00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:46.848
Prithvi Pal ordered the police to open fire on
the advancing crowd, killing three.

15
00:01:47.128 --> 00:01:52.720
The heavily outnumbered police fell back to
the shelter of the town chowki.

16
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.983
The crowd set the chowki ablaze,

17
00:01:56.043 --> 00:02:00.608
killing all the policemen trapped inside,
including Gupteshwar Singh.

18
00:02:00.888 --> 00:02:07.200
Reports vary on the police retreat: some
constables ran out of ammunition.

19
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.116
Others claimed the crowd's unexpectedly
assertive reaction

20
00:02:11.176 --> 00:02:14.344
to the gunfire caused the retreat.

21
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.987
Nehru and most Congress workers,

22
00:02:22.047 --> 00:02:28.400
in prison when Gandhi decided, felt the
decision was hasty and incorrect.

23
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:35.424
The Moplah Rebellion of 1921 had veered away
from non-violent methods.

24
00:02:35.704 --> 00:02:38.032
In 1921, the Prince

25
00:02:38.092 --> 00:02:45.256
of Wales riots saw a Hindu-Muslim mob attack
Parsis, Jews and Anglo-Indians.

26
00:02:45.536 --> 00:02:51.704
Gandhi did not want the movement to degenerate
into a contest of violence.

27
00:02:51.984 --> 00:02:56.942
Although he had stopped the national revolt
single-handedly,

28
00:02:57.002 --> 00:03:01.392
Gandhi was arrested on 12 February 1922.

29
00:03:01.672 --> 00:03:10.600
On 18 March 1922, he was imprisoned for six
years for publishing seditious materials.

30
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.688
This led to the suppression of the movement
and the arrest of other leaders.

31
00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:25.324
Several raids were conducted and hundreds of
people were arrested.

32
00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:30.044
Six of the accused died while in police
custody.

33
00:03:30.324 --> 00:03:38.076
170 were convicted and 47 were acquitted after
an eight-month trial.

34
00:03:38.356 --> 00:03:43.156
Two of the accused were sentenced to two
years' imprisonment.

35
00:03:43.436 --> 00:03:51.260
On 30 April 1923, the High Court of Allahabad
pronounced the final judgements.

36
00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:58.980
Nineteen demonstrators received death
sentences and 14 received life imprisonment.

37
00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.948
The court reviewed the appeals of the 170
convicted accused.

38
00:04:05.228 --> 00:04:12.836
The 19 condemned to death were hanged between
2 and 11 July 1923.

39
00:04:21.588 --> 00:04:26.361
In 1971, local inhabitants formed an
association

40
00:04:26.421 --> 00:04:30.564
named Chauri Chaura Shaheed Smarak Samiti.

41
00:04:30.844 --> 00:04:39.556
In 1973, this Samiti constructed near the lake
a 12.2-metre-tall triangular minaret.

42
00:04:39.836 --> 00:04:45.932
Each side of the minaret depicts a figure
hanging with a noose around his neck.

43
00:04:46.212 --> 00:04:54.180
The minaret was built at a cost of Rs 13,500
contributed by popular subscription.

44
00:04:54.460 --> 00:05:02.380
A memorial to the dead policemen was dedicated
by the British colonial authorities in 1923.

45
00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:09.620
Nehru described the movement as ending
suddenly on 4 February 1922.
